# Project Guardrails (AI Workflow)

Full reference: [`PROJECT_GUARDRAILS.md`](../../PROJECT_GUARDRAILS.md). Recovery systems already exist under `docs/foundation/` and `scripts/recovery/` — **integrate, do not recreate**.

## Scope

- Modify **only** systems named in the user request.
- One feature module per task when possible — see `docs/workflow/FEATURE_ISOLATION.md`.
- `mobile-only` tasks: touch mobile branches only — `docs/workflow/MOBILE_FIRST_DEVELOPMENT.md`.

## Protected (do not change without explicit scope)

Hero/cinematic shell (`src/app/page.js`), 2MRRW branding, navigation, subscribe page, cart/checkout flows, `AuthContext`, playback (`AudioContext`, `GlobalAudioPlayerBar`), modals/animations (`framer-motion`, `useReducedMotion`, `data-cinematic-video`), `VaultUnlockedRoom`, recovery docs/scripts/anchor, mobile shell when not scoped.

## Recovery before rebuild

- Dry-run: `npm run recover:foundation -- --dry-run`
- Full local restore: `npm run recover:foundation`
- Verify: `npm run verify:foundation`
- Prefer selective file restore over full rollback — `docs/workflow/SELECTIVE_RESTORATION_WORKFLOW.md`

## Constraints

- No UI redesign unless explicitly requested.
- No dependency bumps (`next`, `react`, `framer-motion`, `@supabase/*`, `@stripe/*`) without approval.
- Entitlements: webhook → Supabase → `/api/account/state` → UI — never client-side permission overrides.
- Do not commit or deploy unless the user asks.

Also apply: `build-frame-of-mind.mdc`, `frontend-foundation.mdc`, `platform-architecture.mdc`.
